uation is limited to specific benchmarks, and the paper does not provide a broader assessment of LST's generalization capabilities (Section 4.1)."], "suggestions": ["Extend the evaluation to include full-duplex interaction scenarios to demonstrate LST's applicability in real-time dialogue systems (Section 7).", "Explore instruction fine-tuning and downstream adaptation to further validate the practical utility of LST (Section 7).", "Conduct a broader empirical evaluation on additional benchmarks to assess the generalization capabilities of LST (Section 4.1).", "Investigate alignment-free patching strategies to reduce dependency on forced alignments during pre-training (Section 7)."], "rating": 8, "confidence": 5, "soundness": 4, "presentation": 4, "contribution": 4}

